# =============================================================================
#  assets/textures/iso_cover.pix  —  the collection page's cover for Iso Farm
# =============================================================================
#  Chapter 145 gave `iso` and `colony` manifests, which put them on the page you
#  send someone — and that page REFUSES to show a card with no picture, because a
#  silently blank panel is indistinguishable from a game that has no art.
#
#  So they needed covers, and a cover has to come through one of the four doors
#  like every other `.hrt`. This is `asset.pixels`: art we drew. The shapes are laid
#  out by the game's OWN projection — a tile at (col,row) sits at
#  x = 32 + (col-row)*9, y = 20 + (col+row)*5, the same diamond `iso_render` walks —
#  so the cover is the game's geometry rather than a picture of it. Three tiles are
#  raised, which is what a built farm looks like from here.
#
#  Deliberately NOT a screenshot. Baking a frame of a running game would be a FIFTH
#  door into `.hrt`, and a fifth door is a decision with its own chapter, not a
#  side effect of needing two thumbnails.
#
#  Re-bake after editing:
#      ./build/demo --cmd asset.pixels textures/iso_cover.pix textures/iso_cover.hrt
# =============================================================================

size 64
grid 1 1

palette . 1b1f2aff     # the sky behind the grid
palette g 6f9a5aff     # a tile's top face
palette G 5d8449ff     # ...the darker half of the checker
palette r c98a4bff     # a RAISED tile's top — tilled earth
palette R a06c39ff     # ...its side wall, in shadow

tile 0
